a function $y=f(x)$ with period $4$ is shown above. What is the graph of $y=f(x)$ on the interval $-6\\le x\\le 6?$"] ["question-81171e25-e5ad-5118-af05-1058347bd84c" :question/worked-solution "The graph above shows the function in the interval $-2\\le x\\le 2.$\n\nSince this interval has length $4,$ and the period of the function is also $4,$ this interval represents a single period of the function.\n\nTherefore, the function will consist of many copies of the shape shown above, shifted horizontally by multiples of $4.$\n\n![](images/13/13eb143d92cd215f9283a44ad67ca91e679610d4b6625ae53ced56295430e843.png)"] ["question-81171e25-e5ad-5118-af05-1058347bd84c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-bbb74983-a5fb-5b54-80ff-62e42e368833" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbb74983-a5fb-5b54-80ff-62e42e368833"] ["answer-c7264fca-3bea-51fc-9e5c-4c009f2fe062" :answer/id #uuid "c7264fca-3bea-51fc-9e5c-4c009f2fe062"] ["answer-c7264fca-3bea-51fc-9e5c-4c009f2fe062" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-c7264fca-3bea-51fc-9e5c-4c009f2fe062" :answer/value "images/13/13eb143d92cd215f9283a44ad67ca91e679610d4b6625ae53ced56295430e843.png"] ["answer-c9f360fa-fc4a-5b06-96ff-4de49594a49d" :answer/id #uuid "c9f360fa-fc4a-5b06-96ff-4de49594a49d"] ["answer-c9f360fa-fc4a-5b06-96ff-4de49594a49d" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-c9f360fa-fc4a-5b06-96ff-4de49594a49d" :answer/value "images/19/192c95fa84b2a10e8131417d8aa8f27cfec426e304a8a5e5424eebf8b77f61cb.png"] ["answer-146ab018-a035-5b73-95a8-05742d6e5827" :answer/id #uuid "146ab018-a035-5b73-95a8-05742d6e5827"] ["answer-146ab018-a035-5b73-95a8-05742d6e5827" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-146ab018-a035-5b73-95a8-05742d6e5827" :answer/value "images/40/40e6d09505869a58f24671706f86c47089b9d8063f9cecaf8c4c24c4e6c939d3.png"] ["answer-0638622e-b7c3-5da8-a7c5-6cb908cc9ef1" :answer/id #uuid "0638622e-b7c3-5da8-a7c5-6cb908cc9ef1"] ["answer-0638622e-b7c3-5da8-a7c5-6cb908cc9ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answ